"""
Live changes. Subscriptions run only over the graphql-transport-ws WebSocket on /graphql; queries
and mutations run only over HTTP POST on /graphql.

A subscription delivers changes from the moment it registers. It sends no snapshot and replays
nothing missed. To build current state, subscribe first, then run the queries the field names,
and apply each later change by id. For library administration, query
`libraries { id name status scanStartedOn scanCompletedOn }`. Library-content subscriptions complete
when their library is removed, or if it is already absent when they register. Other subscriptions
do not normally complete while the server runs.

A field error does not end the operation. When a selected field of one change fails to resolve,
the server still delivers the change with the failed value as null and with errors, and later
changes still arrive. A later change may not repeat a value that failed. After a change that
carries errors, the client applies its usable portions according to the field's payload policy
and runs the field's queries again while the subscription stays open. A field may define an
atomic unit whose existing cached values are preserved when its selected fragment is incomplete;
unaffected independent items still apply.

Each field states who may subscribe. These errors end the operation:
PROFILE_REQUIRED when the field needs a selected Profile and the access token has none,
FORBIDDEN when the caller may not subscribe to the field,
AUTHORIZATION_UNAVAILABLE when authorization cannot be decided,
SUBSCRIPTION_OVERFLOW when changes arrived faster than the server could resolve them,
TOO_MANY_OPERATIONS when the connection already runs its maximum number of operations.
After SUBSCRIPTION_OVERFLOW, subscribe again and run the field's queries again.
"""
type Subscription {
    """
    A library's status or scan times changed. Delivers the library after each change, or null with
    errors when a selected field fails to resolve. ServerAdmin only.

    Each library administration field delivers one library's changes in the order they were
    committed. There is no order across libraries or across fields: `libraryAdded` and
    `libraryStatusChanged` for one library may arrive in either order. This field delivers the
    library as the server reads it after the change, so a client may miss an intermediate status,
    but the last change it receives carries the latest status.
    """
    libraryStatusChanged: Library

    """
    A library was added. Delivers the new library, or null with errors when a selected field fails
    to resolve. ServerAdmin only.
    """
    libraryAdded: Library

    """
    A library was removed. Delivers the removed library's id, or null with errors when a selected
    field fails to resolve. ServerAdmin only.
    """
    libraryRemoved: LibraryRemoval

    """
    The selected Profile's watch state changed. The Profile comes from the access token that opened
    the socket; no argument names the Profile. The caller needs a selected Profile and the
    ViewProfileActivity permission for that Profile. The selected Profile has the permission while
    its Account is enabled.

    Delivers one change for each committed write. The change holds each movie or episode whose watchStatus, watchProgress or
    lastWatchedAt changed. It also holds the season and the series of each such episode, because
    their aggregate values may have changed. Every open socket of the Profile receives the change,
    including the socket of the client that made the write. Values are current values, not
    differences, so a client may apply a change twice. The server reads the values when it delivers
    the change, and it delivers one operation's changes in order, so the last change an operation
    receives carries the latest values.

    To build current state, subscribe first, then query `continueWatching` and the library views
    the client shows. Select the same fields in the change as in those queries. For Continue
    Watching, select continueWatching { itemId edge { cursor orderKey node { ... } } } alongside
    items. The edge uses the same membership and ordering as the query. Merge by ID, compare
    opaque orderKey values and retain the client's shelf cap without backfill. An eligible
    displayed item moved to the tail stays while it fits that cap. Remove only an explicitly
    null edge with no error affecting that change's response path, including aliases and list
    indices. A non-null edge with a null node is not a removal.

    A field that fails to resolve does not end the operation. The `errors` of the message name the
    path of each failed field. A failed nullable field arrives as null. A failed non-null field of
    an item makes that item null, and the other items arrive intact. A change whose items cannot be
    resolved arrives as null.
    """
    watchStateChanged: WatchStateChange
}

"One committed watch-state change for the selected Profile."
type WatchStateChange {
    """
    The movies and episodes whose watch state changed, and the seasons and series that hold those
    episodes. Each item appears once. An item is null when one of its non-null fields failed to
    resolve.
    """
    items: [WatchStateItem]!
    """
    Continue Watching membership for every touched movie or episode, independent of
    the client's shelf cap. Entity updates remain available through items.
    """
    continueWatching: [ContinueWatchingChange]!
}

"A touched item's current membership in the selected Profile's Continue Watching list."
type ContinueWatchingChange {
    itemId: ID!
    """
    The same edge returned by the query, or null when the item no longer belongs.
    Remove membership only for an explicitly resolved null edge with no error whose
    response path starts at this change, including aliases and list indices. A
    non-null edge with a null node is never a removal. Preserve affected cached
    fields and membership until shared recovery; usable sibling changes may apply.
    """
    edge: ContinueWatchingEdge
}
